From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 07 Oct 2026 10:47:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: program the beacon rate again after a full reset

The driver caches the rate of the beacon rate table and skips the
table command when the rate does not change. A full reset reloads the
firmware, which drops the table, but the cache keeps its value. When
mac80211 restores the beacons, the driver does not program the table,
and the beacons use the entry that the reloaded firmware has by
default. The 6 GHz LPI beacon rate is in the same table.

Clear the cache in the full reset, so that the beacon restore programs
the table again.

Fixes: af41374a3b8e ("wifi: mt76: connac: add beacon duplicate TX mode support for mt7996")
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/mac.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -2378,6 +2378,8 @@ mt7996_mac_full_reset(struct mt7996_dev
 	mt7996_for_each_phy(dev, phy) {
 		phy->omac_mask = 0;
 		phy->csa_quiet_links = 0;
+		/* the reloaded firmware has no beacon rate table */
+		phy->beacon_rate = -1;
 		mt76_phy_tx_unblock(phy->mt76, MT76_TX_BLOCK_CSA);
 	}
 	dev->mld_idx_mask = 0;
